 "description": "A thicket-forming evergreen shrub of the redwood forest and the foggy north-facing scrub, spreading by underground stems into dense patches. Its leaves are large, leathery and shiny, and its dark purple berries hang in rows below the leaves in late summer.",
 "season_notes": {
  "winter": "Leathery leaves stay green, some bronzing where the sun reaches them; deer browse it hard.",
  "spring": "Bright new shoots and rows of white-pink urn flowers on reddish stalks.",
  "summer": "Flowering ends and the hairy fruits swell and darken.",
  "fall": "Dark blue-black berries hang along the stems into December."
